    2. Assign L distinct colors to main_run pixels. Place run flush with edge.
    3. Cast 4-diagonal rays from each main pixel in order; record the ray grid (with occlusion).
    4. Identify diagonal-connected bg regions in the ray grid. Pick 1-2 regions that touch a grid edge (excluding the main_run's flush edge).
    5. For each chosen region, place a size-2 bar (contiguous pair) on the edge within that region; assign a fresh color.
    6. Verify bars' diag-flood regions are disjoint and total colors <= 9.
    7. Input = black grid with only main_run and bar pixels; output = ray grid overlaid with bar floods.
